`packages/font-metrics` depends on harfbuzzjs
(https://github.com/harfbuzz/harfbuzzjs), MIT License, for the pinned
HarfBuzz WebAssembly text-shaping runtime exposed by the opt-in Node
`@injoffice/font-metrics/harfbuzz` entry.

The complete harfbuzzjs MIT license is reproduced below.

`packages/font-metrics` also depends on bidi-js 1.0.3
(https://github.com/lojjic/bidi-js), MIT License, for its pinned,
source-digest-verified Unicode Bidirectional Algorithm 13.0.0 implementation.
The complete bidi-js MIT license is reproduced below.

bidi-js declares require-from-string 2.0.2
(https://github.com/floatdrop/require-from-string) as a runtime dependency.
InjOffice pins that transitive dependency exactly; its MIT license is reproduced
below.

`scripts/unicode13/ucd` contains the exact Unicode Character Database 13.0.0
Scripts, PropList, DerivedCoreProperties, UnicodeData, and DerivedAge sources.
The checked generator produces the compact Script/Common/Inherited,
White_Space, punctuation, Default_Ignorable/control, and assigned-repertoire
tables shared by native itemization, shaping, and bidi admission. Every source,
the projection, generator, and runtime encoding is SHA-256-bound. Copyright ©
2019-2020 Unicode, Inc. The data is distributed under Unicode License v3,
reproduced in `/LICENSE-UNICODE.txt`.

`packages/pdf` depends on `pngjs` (https://github.com/lukeapage/pngjs),
MIT License, for PNG decode/encode in `image/decodePng.ts` and
`ocr/encodePng.ts`.

`packages/pdf/src/ocr` (vision-LLM OCR — page rasterization and the
invisible-text-layer splice) is InjOffice code.

